From ea3247e74485e6a177e8315464038b11858ddb65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:36:21 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): drag a part along an axis with move handles

#1198 slice b. The bottom bar gains a Move mode button; with it on, the
one selected part wears three axis arms ending in balls, a constant size
on screen. Pressing a ball wins over orbit and pick; dragging previews
the part sliding along that axis (view state only) and the release
queues one MoveModelBy, which the drain runs as the Model page's own
MoveModel with the rotation kept bit for bit - one undo step per drag.
Escape mid-drag and a zero-length drag add no history step. In a setup
that holds the part turned, the part moves along the axis shown.

Refs #1198

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
